## Scenarios

### Configuration and Environment Access

#### round-trips an environment variable through set and get

- Set SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE then read it back
   - Expected: rt_env_set("SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE", "probe-value") is true
   - Expected: rt_env_get("SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE") equals `probe-value`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-CONFIG-ENV-001
step("Set SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE then read it back")
expect(rt_env_set("SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE", "probe-value")).to_equal(true)
expect(rt_env_get("SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_PROBE")).to_equal("probe-value")
```

</details>

#### reads an existing platform environment variable

- Read PATH from the host environment
   - Expected: path contains `/`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-CONFIG-ENV-001
step("Read PATH from the host environment")
val path = rt_env_get("PATH") ?? ""
expect(path.contains("/")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### returns nil for a missing environment variable

- Read a variable that was never set


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-CONFIG-ENV-001
step("Read a variable that was never set")
expect(rt_env_get("SIMPLE_CONFIG_ENV_DEFINITELY_MISSING_20260822")).to_be_nil()
```

</details>

